        <item>
            <title>2.40.0</title>
            <pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 01:01:14 +0900</pubDate>
            <link>https://github.com/Saqoosha/Canopy</link>
            <sparkle:version>128</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.40.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>15.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[### Features
- **SSH remote sessions survive a host reboot.** When the remote CLI dies mid-conversation (host restart, network drop), the pane now reconnects on its own and resumes the same conversation with its full context instead of closing. The retry budget is bounded, so a host that stays down ends in a "reconnect failed" overlay rather than a loop. Known limit: the resumed pane's scrollback shows "Loading…" until you send a message — the model already has the context.
- **"Continue session" works on native Windows hosts** (Git Bash over SSH): `C:\` drive paths are now encoded the way the Windows CLI encodes them, so previous sessions are found and `/resume` lands on the right transcript.

### Bug Fixes
- The sidebar open/close button no longer comes up in the wrong place — drawn over the first pane's header — and unresponsive after a Save-and-Quit restore launch on macOS 27. Cmd+Opt+S still worked; the button did not.
- The "session failed to start" banner is cleared the next time you deliberately open a launcher (Cmd+N, Cmd+click New Session, closing the last pane). It used to persist until you dismissed it by hand and could surface on a New Session pane opened hours after the failure.
]]></description>
